WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.601
-A member of the committee

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:05.300
investigating
the January 6th insurrection

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.968
revealed what he called the most
chilling moment from that day,

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:09.701
while three more Trump allies,

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.767
including Kevin McCarthy
and Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:14.267
were caught lying about their
roles in the attempted coup.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:17.601
Oh, and also, Donald Trump said,
in a lawsuit,

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.868
that he's afraid of getting hit
with dangerous fruits.

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:22.000
[ Laughter ]
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.300
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.133
Every day, it seems like we get

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:29.968
more bombshell reporting
about what happened

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.868
on January 6th
and who was involved

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:33.934
and now, on top of everything
else we've already learned,

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:35.334
we have what one member

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.534
of the committee investigating
the insurrection called

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:39.501
the most chilling
anecdote yet --

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:41.834
an account of something
Vice President Mike Pence said

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:44.200
in the Capitol
as the riot was unfolding.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.634
-Democratic Representative
Jamie Raskin of Maryland,

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:49.234
who is a member of the House
1/6 select committee,

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:51.567
said the committee's
upcoming public hearings will

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:54.767
"tell a story that will really
blow the roof off the House."

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.534
At an event in Washington, D.C.,

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:59.067
Raskin spoke about what he
called a chilling moment

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:00.534
from January the 6th,

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:03.267
involving former
Vice President Mike Pence.

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:05.868
After rioters stormed
the halls of Congress,

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:08.334
some chanting,
"Hang Mike Pence,"

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.534
the vice president's
Secret Service agents rushed him

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:13.133
to a secure location
inside the Capitol.

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.567
Those agents, who, Raskin says,

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:17.234
he suspects were reporting

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:19.601
to Trump's
Secret Service agents,

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:22.834
then tried to whisk Pence
away from the Capitol.

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:24.067
That's when,
the congressman says,

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:25.400
Pence uttered what he called

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.000
"the six most chilling words"
he's heard

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.701
throughout this
entire investigation --

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:32.467
"I'm not getting in that car."

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:35.334
-I'm guessing that's when Pence
went into full chameleon mode.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:37.801
You know that thing he does
where he closes his eyes

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:39.501
[ Laughter ]
and sits totally still,

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:41.467
hoping no one will notice him?

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.434
[ As Pence ]
This is not happening.

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:45.000
[ Laughter ]
You are not here.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.667
You are in your happy place,

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:48.868
at a public library,

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:51.033
burning a pile
of "Harry Potter" books.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:51.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.200
That's how nefarious

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.100
this plot was,
and how deep it went --

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.534
Trump's own vice president

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:58.634
suspected the Secret Service
might be involved.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:01.434
Almost every day, it seems,
more evidence emerges

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:04.033
that implicates yet another
member of Trump's inner circle

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.400
and, nearly every day,

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.334
those same people
get caught lying about it.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:10.000
Like Trump's former energy
secretary Rick Perry,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.767
who denied to CNN
that he ever proposed ideas

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:14.400
to Trump's chief of staff
Mark Meadows

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.334
for how to overturn
the election results,

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:18.100
before text messages turned up

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.934
in which Perry was caught
saying exactly that.

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:23.834
And Perry even went
out of his way to make clear

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:26.634
he was the one writing
the text messages.

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:29.267
-Trump's former
energy secretary Rick Perry,

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:32.300
former governor of Texas,
texted Meadows...

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:43.901
Just for the record,
previously,

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:46.868
we've reported at CNN
another Rick Perry text.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.968
He denied it.
It was his phone.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.701
CNN has confirmed,
from multiple sources,

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:53.534
friends and colleagues of his,

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:56.601
that that is his phone number
these texts were coming from.

00:02:56.601 --> 00:03:00.133
In fact, these texts
on the Meadows log show

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:01.367
that he signed his name

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:03.033
[ Laughter ]
and his telephone number

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:05.801
at the end of the text.

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:07.934
-I think, if you're going
to pitch ideas for a coup,

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:10.467
then lie about it, maybe don't
sign your text messages

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:12.801
with your name and phone number.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.667
Did he also send a follow-up
text that said...

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:19.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:20.767
I will say,
if you've ever texted

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.634
with an older person,
like a parent or an in-law,

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:23.968
you've probably witnessed
the same behavior.

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:26.400
They all sign their text
messages with their names,

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.534
like they're writing
Civil War letters home.

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:29.267
[ Laughter ]
[ Southern accent ]

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:32.200
[ Poignant tune plays ]

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:41.434
♪♪

00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:51.434
♪♪

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:55.534
♪♪

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:57.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:57.968 --> 00:04:00.334
The circle of Trump cronies
involved in the coup

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:02.667
keeps getting wider and wider,
to the point where it seems

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:05.367
like virtually the entirety
of the Trump administration

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:07.300
and his closest allies
in Congress

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.267
were involved in some way.

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:09.634
Like Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.801
who we now know
was also texting Meadows,

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.601
more than a week
after the insurrection,

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:15.267
about the possibility of Trump

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:17.467
declaring martial law
to stay in power,

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:19.534
an idea that had been advocated
by Trump allies

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:21.133
like Michael Flynn
and Mike Lindell,

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:23.901
only Greene misspelled
the word martial

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:25.501
in the dumbest possible way.

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:27.234
-Three days
before the inauguration,

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:29.868
Marjorie Taylor Greene
sent this text message

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:31.334
to Mark Meadows...

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.234
Note on your screen,
she misspells the word martial.

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:47.133
That's right. She spelled it
like the name Marshall.

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:49.033
[ Laughter ]
Now, in her defense,
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:50.467
probably just confused
martial law

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:51.701
with Marshalls law,

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:53.000
[ Laughter ]
which she violates

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.300
every time she tries
to bring more

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.801
than six items
into the changing room,

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:57.868
at which point she's escorted
from the store, screaming --

00:04:57.868 --> 00:04:59.567
[ As Greene ]
It's my constitutional right

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:02.200
to find comfortable slacks
at a reasonable price!

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.467
[ Laughter ]
And then last night,

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:06.868
in an interview with Fox News
host Laura Ingraham,

00:05:06.868 --> 00:05:09.100
Greene implied that the
text messages in question

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.534
might not even be hers,

00:05:10.534 --> 00:05:13.234
while also insisting that,
if they were hers,

00:05:13.234 --> 00:05:16.167
she wasn't actually asking
Trump to declare martial law.

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:17.601
She was just letting him know

00:05:17.601 --> 00:05:19.667
that it was something
that was being discussed.

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:22.567
-Those are reportedly
my text messages.

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:25.133
I think, if people read them
for themself,

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:26.767
if those were my text messages,

00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:29.634
they clearly say that I
wasn't calling for that.

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:32.901
I actually said that's something
I don't know about.

00:05:32.901 --> 00:05:34.934
That was what those
text messages say.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.501
-So you didn't advocate --
-Right now, there's a group --

00:05:36.501 --> 00:05:38.200
-You never advocated
martial law,

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:41.234
that President Trump
should use martial law

00:05:41.234 --> 00:05:43.701
to stop, you know,
the transition of power?

00:05:43.701 --> 00:05:45.434
You never advocated
for that, did you?

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:49.801
[ Laughter ]
-I don't recall ever advocating
for martial law.

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:51.501
I think --
I don't know if you have that

00:05:51.501 --> 00:05:52.868
up on the screen right now

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:54.200
because I can't see it...
-No.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.701
-...but, if you put
that text message up,

00:05:56.701 --> 00:05:58.601
it's clear and easy to read

00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:00.634
that, if that's my text messages

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:01.901
and that's what
they're reporting,

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:04.634
I don't recall if they are,
but if they are,

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:09.367
those text messages do not say
calling for martial law.

00:06:09.367 --> 00:06:12.901
-So you don't know if the texts,
which you've seen,

00:06:12.901 --> 00:06:14.567
were actually yours.

00:06:14.567 --> 00:06:15.934
You sound like a werewolf trying

00:06:15.934 --> 00:06:17.968
to piece things together
the next morning.

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:20.601
[ Laughter ]
"Look, I don't recall
eating any villagers,

00:06:20.601 --> 00:06:22.834
but if that's why there's blood
on my nightshirt,

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:25.000
then I guess I forgot
to chain myself to the bed."

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.501
Also, can we go back to this?

00:06:27.501 --> 00:06:29.767
-I don't know if you have that
up on the screen right now

00:06:29.767 --> 00:06:31.000
because I can't see it.
-No.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.734
-I like that she accidentally
asked Ingraham,

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:35.334
"Are you going to do
any journalism?"

00:06:35.334 --> 00:06:36.467
And Ingraham said, "No."

00:06:36.467 --> 00:06:37.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.734 --> 00:06:39.033
Fox News reacts to the question,

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:40.267
"Are you going
to do journalism?"

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:42.501
the way Larry David reacts
to a dinner invite.

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:43.767
[ Changes accent ]
Larry, you want
to come over tonight?

00:06:43.767 --> 00:06:45.133
Come on, I'll drive you.

00:06:45.133 --> 00:06:47.400
[ As David ]
Uh...

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.834
I'm not getting in that car.

00:06:48.834 --> 00:06:50.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.667 --> 00:06:53.534
They all do the same thing --
lie, get caught lying,

00:06:53.534 --> 00:06:55.901
then talk in nonsense
word-salad circles

00:06:55.901 --> 00:06:57.767
of inscrutable bull[bleep]
to try to get out of it.

00:06:57.767 --> 00:06:58.868
The same thing happened

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:00.367
with House GOP leader
Kevin McCarthy,

00:07:00.367 --> 00:07:03.334
after he denied a report
that he told fellow Republicans,

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:05.567
in the days
after the insurrection,

00:07:05.567 --> 00:07:07.534
that he would urge Trump
to resign.

00:07:07.534 --> 00:07:10.801
And then audio surfaced
of the phone call

00:07:10.801 --> 00:07:13.868
in which McCarthy said
he would urge Trump to resign.

00:07:13.868 --> 00:07:15.968
After the audio surfaced,
McCarthy held a press conference

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:18.100
where he tried to claim
he hadn't lied

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.334
when he denied
the initial report,

00:07:19.334 --> 00:07:21.133
but his answer made
no sense, whatsoever.

00:07:21.133 --> 00:07:22.901
-The reporter never asked me
that question.

00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:23.968
The reporter came to me

00:07:23.968 --> 00:07:25.767
the night before he
released the book

00:07:25.767 --> 00:07:27.567
and my understanding was
he was saying

00:07:27.567 --> 00:07:29.534
that I asked President Trump
to resign.

00:07:29.534 --> 00:07:31.934
No, I never did,
and that's what I was answering.

00:07:31.934 --> 00:07:33.734
If you're answering --
If you're asking now,

00:07:33.734 --> 00:07:36.567
did I tell my members
that we're going to ask,

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:39.334
ask them if I told any of them
that I said President Trump.

00:07:39.334 --> 00:07:40.400
The answer is no.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.834
-Your claim is
that you weren't lying

00:07:41.834 --> 00:07:43.968
when you deny that you said
you would urge Trump to resign

00:07:43.968 --> 00:07:46.667
because the reporter asked you
if you urged Trump to resign,

00:07:46.667 --> 00:07:48.467
which you claim you didn't,

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:51.067
and, if we want to know
if you told your members

00:07:51.067 --> 00:07:54.467
you would urge Trump to resign,
we should ask your members

00:07:54.467 --> 00:07:57.100
if you told them
you would urge him to resign,

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:59.200
instead of just listening
to the audio

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.167
where you told them
you would urge Trump to resign.

00:08:02.167 --> 00:08:04.334
[ Laughter ]
I feel like I just spent an hour

00:08:04.334 --> 00:08:06.868
trying to find an exit
in an M.C. Escher painting.

00:08:06.868 --> 00:08:07.868
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.868 --> 00:08:09.968
Why would we ask your members

00:08:09.968 --> 00:08:10.701
if you said it?

00:08:10.701 --> 00:08:12.133
We have the audio

00:08:12.133 --> 00:08:13.734
of you telling your members

00:08:13.734 --> 00:08:16.300
impeachment would pass
and Trump should resign.

00:08:24.167 --> 00:08:26.534
That wasn't me!
That was my friend...

00:08:26.534 --> 00:08:28.400
[ Laughter ]
Here's my question

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.667
about everything we've learned,
so far.

00:08:29.667 --> 00:08:31.334
In addition to being
horrifying and dangerous,

00:08:31.334 --> 00:08:33.300
why is everything always
so incredibly stupid?

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.767
Has it always been this way?

00:08:34.767 --> 00:08:36.567
Whenever you watch old movies
about politics,

00:08:36.567 --> 00:08:38.167
like "Mr. Smith Goes
to Washington"

00:08:38.167 --> 00:08:39.701
or "All the President's Men,"

00:08:39.701 --> 00:08:41.400
it all seems so noble
and dignified.

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:43.934
I can't imagine there's
old newsreel footage

00:08:43.934 --> 00:08:46.901
of Harry Truman moving around
to a Village People song.

00:08:46.901 --> 00:08:48.400
-♪ It's fun to stay at the ♪

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:50.567
♪ YMCA ♪

00:08:50.567 --> 00:08:52.167
♪ It's fun to stay at the ♪

00:08:52.167 --> 00:08:54.901
♪ YMCA ♪

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:56.400
[ Laughter ]
-For example,
the news found a way

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:57.667
to get even dumber this week,

00:08:57.667 --> 00:09:00.234
when newly released excerpts
from a deposition reveal

00:09:00.234 --> 00:09:02.300
that Donald Trump said
he was afraid

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:04.834
that protesters,
during the 2016 election,

00:09:04.834 --> 00:09:07.767
would throw dangerous fruits
at him during a rally.

00:09:15.868 --> 00:09:18.434
[ Laughter ]

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:22.434
[ Laughter ]

00:09:26.801 --> 00:09:28.367
[ Laughter ]

00:09:30.267 --> 00:09:32.467
[ Laughter ]

00:09:33.901 --> 00:09:36.133
[ As Trump ]
That's -- and that's why we
had the security guards.

00:09:36.133 --> 00:09:37.434
[ Laughter ]
Now, me, I wanted --

00:09:37.434 --> 00:09:40.667
I wanted to use some very highly
specialized fruit ninjas.

00:09:40.667 --> 00:09:42.367
[ Laughter ]
I said, "Let's do ninjas

00:09:42.367 --> 00:09:43.734
because they have
the fruit swords."

00:09:43.734 --> 00:09:45.367
But they said no because,

00:09:45.367 --> 00:09:47.467
if they miss three fruits,
they're out and you can't --

00:09:47.467 --> 00:09:49.100
[ Laughter ]

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:50.634
You can't show weakness
like that.

00:09:50.634 --> 00:09:53.000
[ Laughter ]
And then there's this,
even dumber,

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.567
part of the deposition,
where Trump says...

00:09:56.567 --> 00:09:59.934
[ Laughter ]

00:10:05.534 --> 00:10:08.067
[ Laughter ]

00:10:08.067 --> 00:10:09.701
What do you mean, do fruit?

00:10:09.701 --> 00:10:10.901
[ Laughter ]

00:10:10.901 --> 00:10:12.601
What do you mean,
you were put on alert?

00:10:12.601 --> 00:10:15.033
There's an alert system
for fruit?

00:10:15.033 --> 00:10:17.267
It's like the Homeland Security
threat level.

00:10:17.267 --> 00:10:19.767
Red's tomato,
yellow's for banana,

00:10:19.767 --> 00:10:20.467
and green is for

00:10:20.467 --> 00:10:21.634
[ As Trump ] avocado.

00:10:21.634 --> 00:10:24.634
[ Laughter ]
And you know what they say --

00:10:24.634 --> 00:10:26.467
If you get hit with an avocado,

00:10:26.467 --> 00:10:27.734
you're toast.

00:10:27.734 --> 00:10:29.567
[ Laughter ]

00:10:29.567 --> 00:10:31.434
And that's today's brunch joke.

00:10:31.434 --> 00:10:32.567
[ Laughter ]
[ Clink ]

00:10:32.567 --> 00:10:34.801
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:10:34.801 --> 00:10:35.534
Thank you.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:42.234
Also, how would somebody
sneak a pineapple

00:10:42.234 --> 00:10:44.167
into a political rally?

00:10:44.167 --> 00:10:45.868
[ Laughter ]
"Oh, you misheard.

00:10:45.868 --> 00:10:48.234
This isn't a pineapple.

00:10:48.234 --> 00:10:49.167
This is my baby.

00:10:49.167 --> 00:10:50.901
